This heading covers hats and other headgear (whether or not lined or trimmed) made directly by knitting or crocheting (whether or not fulled or felted) or made up from lace, felt or other textile fabric in the piece (whether or not the fabric has been impregnated, coated or covered with oil, wax, rubber or other materials).

The heading includes hat-shapes made by sewing, but excludes hat-shapes or hats made by sewing together plaits or assembled strips (heading 65.04). It also covers felt hats and other felt headgear made from the hat bodies, hoods or plateaux of heading 65.01, including hoods which have been blocked or have had their brims defined.

The articles falling in this heading may be lined or trimmed.

The heading includes :

(1) blocked hoods and capelines of felt;
(2) berets, bonnets, hoods and the like, usually knitted or crocheted directly to shape;
(3) certain oriental headwear (e.g., fezzes), usually knitted or crocheted and fulled;
(4) peaked caps of all kinds;
(5) professional or ecclesiastical headgear (mitres, birettas, mortar-boards, etc.);
(6) chefs' hats, nuns' veils, nurses' caps, waitresses' caps, etc.;
(7) pith or cork helmets covered with textile fabric;
(8) sou'westers;
(9) hoods presented separately (but excluding hoods detachable from cloaks, coats, etc., which are classified with the garment according to their constituent material);
(10) top hats and opera hats.

The heading also covers hair-nets and snoods of any material (usually tulle, net, knitted or crocheted fabrics, or human hair).

This heading covers all headgear not classified in the preceding headings of this Chapter or in Chapter 63, 68 or 95. It covers, in particular, safety headgear (e.g., helmets for sports, military or fire brigade use, motorcycle riders, miners, construction workers), whether or not fitted with protective padding, and sometimes fitted with microphones or earphones.

The heading also covers :

(1) Headgear of rubber or plastics (e.g., bathing caps, hoods);

(2) Headgear of leather or composition leather;

(3) Headgear of furskin or artificial fur;

(4) Headgear of feathers or artificial flowers;

(5) Headgear of metal.

